  "id": "cytomegalovirus",
  "term": "cytomegalovirus",
  "definition": "Cytomegalovirus is a common virus that can cause infections around the time of birth. In infants, infection may be present from birth or acquired after the first 3 weeks of life, often through breast milk, and it is usually without symptoms in full-term infants but can cause serious illness in preterm or very low birth weight infants.",
